# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — never commit real keys.

# ── Contact form ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Web3Forms access key. Get one free in about 30 seconds, no account needed:
#   https://web3forms.com/  →  enter the destination email  →  key is emailed
#
# Whatever address you register the key against is where enquiries land, so
# point it at your own inbox while this is a demo and swap it for Travis's
# address on handover.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the client, and this key
# is public by design (it is visible in the built JS). It is a routing token,
# not a secret — it can only submit to the inbox it was registered against.
#
# With this unset the form deliberately disables its submit button and says so,
# rather than silently swallowing a real enquiry.
VITE_W3F_KEY=
